# Contracts

> The promises between parts of {{PROJECT_NAME}}. If two components are built by
> different activities or different teams, their contract lives here.

## 1. Contract inventory

| Contract          | Producer       | Consumer       | Transport        | Version |
| ----------------- | -------------- | -------------- | ---------------- | ------- |
| {{CONTRACT_NAME}} | {{PRODUCER}}   | {{CONSUMER}}   | {{TRANSPORT}}    | v1      |

A contract without a consumer is not a contract; delete it.

## 2. Shape

For each contract, document:

- **Request / input** — required and optional fields, types, limits.
- **Response / output** — shape, pagination, empty cases.
- **Errors** — the error taxonomy, status/error codes, retryability.
- **Idempotency** — which operations are safe to repeat.
- **Authentication / authorization** — who may call it and with what token.
- **Versioning** — how a breaking change is introduced and retired.

