## 4. Compatibility rules

- Additive changes are allowed: new optional fields, new endpoints.
- Removing or renaming a field is breaking; it needs a new version and an ADR.
- Consumers must ignore unknown fields.
- A contract change updates this document **and** the generated API docs in the
  same activity.

## 5. Ownership and review

- Each contract has an owner (the producing activity or team).
- A contract change is reviewed by a consumer, not only by the producer.
- The OpenAPI/IDL/schema file is the machine-readable source; this document is
  the human-readable rationale.

